<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel shares up on debt hopes.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel shares up on debt hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Eurotunnel jumped on Monday after the Channel Tunnel operator reported higher traffic for 1996 and said it hoped to complete negotiating details of a bank debt accord in March.</p>
<p>Chairman Patrick Ponsolle told Reuters he expected the details of a bank debt deal to be set by March. Eurotunnel said it had 13 million passengers in 1996 and revenues of about 450 million sterling.</p>
<p>&quot;The travel figures and the news of the debt talks was very good,&quot; a broker said. The share was up 6.52 percent at 7.35 francs at 1430 GMT.</p>
</text>
